Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:41:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] sync: device secret of the sync account (K3, #977 C1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Format from #977 at 60cc1d0 (cuenta/README.md «Secreto de aparato»): the
server gives each device a «secreto» (base64url of 32 bytes) in
alta/confirmar, entrar/terminar and aparatos/renovar without «aparato».
The client keeps it encrypted with OSCrypt like the token and sends it,
with «aparato», in aparatos/renovar, contrasena/cambiar and
cadena/cambiar, so the server can tell the real author (S3) and an
attacker with only the chain cannot take this device's token.

Replaces the client-side generation of the previous patch. A renewal
answered «credenciales» forgets the device; the next poll adds the Mac
again, with its «Mac añadido» warning.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
